  "id": "fatigue-effect",
  "term": "fatigue effect",
  "definition": "Fatigue effect refers to the changes in behavior and brain functioning that appear when fatigue is induced. In this source, it specifically describes central fatigue produced by prolonged sleep deprivation, with longer exposure linked to anxiety and degenerative changes in the hippocampus.",
